.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_combination" "fuzzygene_combination"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_combination \- Non-additive (synergy / antagonism) analysis of a two gene combination.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_combination(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
\fBgeneA\fR as string, 
\fBgeneB\fR as string, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "knockout", 
\fBsteps\fR as integer = 60, 
\fBtop\fR as integer = 50, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Non-additive (synergy / antagonism) analysis of a two gene combination.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained (or restored) model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgeneA\fB \fR\- the first target gene. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgeneB\fB \fR\- the second target gene; must differ from \fBgeneA\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- \fBknockout\fR (default), \fBknockdown\fR or \fBoverexpression\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsteps\fB \fR\- iteration budget of each solve. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtop\fB \fR\- number of genes kept in \fBtop\fR and \fBtrajectory\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a named list of data.frames
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Additive expectation is `control + (A - control) + (B - control)`; the non additive
 effect is `joint - additive`. Positive means synergy, negative means antagonism.
 


 


 Returns a named list:
 


 
- \fBsummary\fR: one row with the two genes and \fBmax_abs_non_additive\fR;
- \fBtable\fR: the full 18k gene table \fBgene\fR / \fBsingle_a\fR / \fBsingle_b\fR /
 \fBjoint\fR / \fBadditive\fR / \fBnon_additive\fR;
- \fBtop\fR: the top genes ranked by \fB|non_additive|\fR;
- \fBtrajectory\fR: the frame level version \fBiteration\fR / \fBgene\fR /
 \fBadditive\fR / \fBjoint\fR / \fBnon_additive\fR, which shows whether the deviation appears
 together with the single perturbations or only later.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
